ply.\n- **Bill text:** this is a single-subject bill. Its operative section bars staff from using a name or pronouns that \"do not align with the pupil's biological sex without written authorization from the pupil's parent or legal guardian.\" That matches every clause of rung 5.\n\nCode will compute this chair as `single-source`, because both passages are on one instrument.\n\n**Coded but not supporting the chair:**\n- **AB 510 (2023-2024) and AB 963 (2021-2022):** he co-sponsored both and voted Aye on both. They are parental bills of rights with many unrelated parts, so I coded the votes `multi-subject`. Each one's name/pronoun clause only declares a parental \"right to determine the names and pronouns used for the child while at school.\" It sets no permission or notice rule for staff, so I coded the bill text `direction-only`.\n- **His 2024 press release:** his quoted words (\"Of course parents should have the right to determine the name and religion of their child…\") are `statement-other`, `direction-only`.\n\n**Judgement calls a reviewer may want to check:**\n- **Term start:** his term start was given as unknown. I coded all the Wisconsin Senate records `in-term` because each roll call lists him as a senator in that session.\n- **Vote count field:** the vote pages print the Ayes and Nays counts apart, with names in between, so a verbatim tally could only be the Ayes count. I used `AYES - 18`, `AYES - 22` and `AYES - 19`.\n- **Two quotes:** I included two quotes, both tiered `direction`. \"Parents, not schools and not health care providers, are best able to make decisions about their children\" is marked not quotable (`off-question`).\n\n`needs_source` is empty.","ttft_ms":25531,"type":"result","duration_ms":55217,"uuid":"02723d8b-c715-45e7-9de8-de063e695ed2","ttft_stream_ms":1904,"time_to_request_ms":72,"first_content_frame_ms":1905,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
